      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.507,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "So let's now add the actual logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 7.68,
          "en": "We could do this in the same store file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.68,
          "end": 11.39,
          "en": "The convention kind of is to use separate files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.39,
          "end": 14.28,
          "en": "for the different features your app might have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.28,
          "end": 17.64,
          "en": "And therefore, here still in the store Redux folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.64,
          "end": 20.28,
          "en": "I will add a favorites JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.28,
          "end": 21.57,
          "en": "but you don't have to create it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.57,
          "end": 24.813,
          "en": "You could manage all the logic in one and the same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.88,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "Still here I have a separate file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 31.35,
          "en": "and in there we create a so-called slice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.35,
          "end": 33.59,
          "en": "That's our Redux Toolkit feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.59,
          "end": 36.43,
          "en": "for defining some state, some data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.43,
          "end": 39.513,
          "en": "and some Actions that should be able to change that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 43.63,
          "en": "We create such a slice by importing a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.63,
          "end": 46.9,
          "en": "from @reeduxjs toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.9,
          "end": 49.243,
          "en": "and that function is called createSlice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.19,
          "end": 53.45,
          "en": "We can then call this createSlice function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.45,
          "end": 56.283,
          "en": "in this favorites JS file in the Redux folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.29,
          "end": 59.92,
          "en": "and we pass our object to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.92,
          "end": 61.96,
          "en": "This function will then return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.96,
          "end": 63.763,
          "en": "which I'll name favoritesSlice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 68.57,
          "en": "Now in this we then have to set a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.57,
          "end": 70.61,
          "en": "Favorites could be the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.61,
          "end": 71.49,
          "en": "This is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.49,
          "end": 73.203,
          "en": "It's an identifier you can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 75.713,
          "en": "And then an initialState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.96000000000001,
          "end": 78.83,
          "en": "And for this I'll set an initialState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.83,
          "end": 82.82,
          "en": "which is our object where I have some ids",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.82,
          "end": 85.68,
          "en": "and my ids here should be an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.68,
          "end": 86.75,
          "en": "So that's my initialState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.75,
          "end": 89.16,
          "en": "I have ids with empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.16,
          "end": 92.37,
          "en": "Now these functions which we need to change that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.37,
          "end": 94.8,
          "en": "are now not added to the initialState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.8,
          "end": 98.88,
          "en": "as we did it with context where we had one context object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.88,
          "end": 103.47999999999999,
          "en": "that had both the data and also the functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.47999999999999,
          "end": 105.28,
          "en": "to change the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.28,
          "end": 107.89,
          "en": "Instead, with Redux we have a separation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.89,
          "end": 111.59,
          "en": "and we now simply have a reducers key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.59,
          "end": 113.8,
          "en": "in our slice object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.8,
          "end": 116.57,
          "en": "And reducers are functions that are used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.57,
          "end": 119.14699999999999,
          "en": "to change our state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.14699999999999,
          "end": 123.5,
          "en": "Therefore, we can add functions here in this object methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.5,
          "end": 126.454,
          "en": "and I'll name my first method addFavorite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.454,
          "end": 130.01,
          "en": "and use this arrow functions in text here to define it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.01,
          "end": 133.12,
          "en": "and every method that you define as a reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.12,
          "end": 137.47,
          "en": "will automatically get the latest state as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.47,
          "end": 140.53,
          "en": "Redux will be calling this method for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.53,
          "end": 142.463,
          "en": "and will give you the latest state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.463,
          "end": 145.623,
          "en": "Therefore, we should accept it as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.73,
          "end": 148.49,
          "en": "So that's function number one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.49,
          "end": 150.1,
          "en": "The second function which I wanna add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.1,
          "end": 152.17000000000002,
          "en": "is the removeFavorite function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.17000000000002,
          "end": 154.64,
          "en": "which also is an a function here for me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.64,
          "end": 157.073,
          "en": "and gets this latest state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.42000000000002,
          "end": 161.56,
          "en": "In these functions we can then change the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.56,
          "end": 165.03,
          "en": "And with just Redux, without Redux Toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.03,
          "end": 168.16,
          "en": "you should do this in a immutable way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.16,
          "end": 169.85,
          "en": "When using Redux Toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.85,
          "end": 172.86,
          "en": "you can mutate your state in immutable way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.86,
          "end": 175.42000000000002,
          "en": "because Redux Toolkit will take care about that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.42000000000002,
          "end": 176.64,
          "en": "under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.64,
          "end": 178.01,
          "en": "That's just a side note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.01,
          "end": 181.62,
          "en": "in case you have worked with just Redux in the past.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.62,
          "end": 185.22,
          "en": "With Redux Toolkit, mutating state is okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.22,
          "end": 186.96,
          "en": "If this doesn't tell you anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 186.96,
          "end": 190.253,
          "en": "you might wanna dive into the official Redux stocks first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.18,
          "end": 194.48,
          "en": "So now with that here we got our addFavorite method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 194.48,
          "end": 198.29,
          "en": "And now here we wanna update our state ids array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.29,
          "end": 200.32999999999998,
          "en": "And in this case, if we add a favorite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 200.32999999999998,
          "end": 202.833,
          "en": "push a new ID onto this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.9,
          "end": 206.64,
          "en": "Now it would be nice if we would get this ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 208.01,
          "en": "as part of this method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.01,
          "end": 211.97,
          "en": "and indeed we can accept a second parameter here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 211.97,
          "end": 213.48,
          "en": "an action parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 213.48,
          "end": 215.71,
          "en": "which can hold an extra payload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 215.71,
          "end": 219.373,
          "en": "which we can pass along when invoking this method later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 220.53,
          "end": 224.91,
          "en": "We can get access to this payload by using action payload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.91,
          "end": 228.06,
          "en": "We use this key because action is our object created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 228.06,
          "end": 229.88,
          "en": "and provided by Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 229.88,
          "end": 233.98,
          "en": "and it uses a payload property to transport any extra data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233.98,
          "end": 236.8,
          "en": "we might attach to this function in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.8,
          "end": 239.603,
          "en": "That's why we have to access action payload here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.47,
          "end": 242.76,
          "en": "And then we could expect that in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.76,
          "end": 244.55,
          "en": "when we invoke this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 244.55,
          "end": 248.09,
          "en": "or when we dispatch this action as it's called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.09,
          "end": 252.22,
          "en": "that we set an ID property on this payload object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.22,
          "end": 254.41,
          "en": "And you will see how to set that property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.41,
          "end": 256.39,
          "en": "in a couple of minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 256.39,
          "end": 258.73,
          "en": "So therefore now we could expect to get this ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 258.73,
          "end": 260.06,
          "en": "on our action payload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 260.06,
          "end": 262.903,
          "en": "And we push this ID to our array of ids.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 264.02,
          "end": 265.66,
          "en": "And here when removing our favorite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 265.66,
          "end": 269.24,
          "en": "we also get such an action with such a payload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 269.24,
          "end": 271.53,
          "en": "and therefore then we could update our ids",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 271.53,
          "end": 273.63,
          "en": "by using the built-in splice method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 273.63,
          "end": 276.823,
          "en": "which can be used to remove our item from an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 277.7,
          "end": 280.17,
          "en": "And we now need to find the index of the item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 280.17,
          "end": 281.22,
          "en": "that we wanna remove",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 281.22,
          "end": 283.623,
          "en": "and that could be done with state ids indexOf,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 285.49,
          "end": 289.67,
          "en": "passing action.payload.id to indexOf",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 289.67,
          "end": 293.2,
          "en": "to get the indexOf the item that should be removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 293.2,
          "end": 295.65,
          "en": "and then two splice as a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 295.65,
          "end": 297.36,
          "en": "We provide the number of items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 297.36,
          "end": 298.96,
          "en": "that we wanna remove in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 298.96,
          "end": 303.96,
          "en": "and we only wanna remove that one item which has this ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 304.24,
          "end": 305.69,
          "en": "That's what we wanna do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 306.55,
          "end": 310.7,
          "en": "So now that's the logic we have here in our favoritesSlice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 310.7,
          "end": 315.053,
          "en": "Now we need to export and expose a couple of things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 315.94,
          "end": 319.653,
          "en": "For example, we want to export favoritesSlice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 320.85,
          "end": 324.57,
          "en": "So this constant here dot reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 324.57,
          "end": 326.47,
          "en": "This is an internal thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 326.47,
          "end": 328.9,
          "en": "but we will be able to then merge this reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 328.9,
          "end": 330.61,
          "en": "into our store later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 330.61,
          "end": 332.463,
          "en": "That's why we have to export it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 333.61,
          "end": 336.47,
          "en": "Besides that we should also export two actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 336.47,
          "end": 337.67,
          "en": "as it's called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 337.67,
          "end": 339.72,
          "en": "To be precise, these two actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 339.72,
          "end": 342.01,
          "en": "so that we can dispatch these actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 342.01,
          "end": 346.71,
          "en": "and invoke these methods from different places of our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 346.71,
          "end": 349.98,
          "en": "For this I will export a constant named addFavorite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 349.98,
          "end": 352.31,
          "en": "though this name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 352.31,
          "end": 355.56,
          "en": "Which points at favoritesSlice.actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 355.56,
          "end": 359.97,
          "en": "which is a property provided by the Redux Toolkit library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 359.97,
          "end": 361.22,
          "en": "dot addFavorite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 361.22,
          "end": 363.223,
          "en": "So which points at this method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 364.17,
          "end": 366.74,
          "en": "And then I will repeat the same thing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 366.74,
          "end": 369.47,
          "en": "with export const removeFavorite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 370.58,
          "end": 374.94,
          "en": "by pointing at favoritesSlice actions removeFavorite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 374.94,
          "end": 378.09,
          "en": "These are the things we should export here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 378.09,
          "end": 382.12,
          "en": "And now as a last step before we can start using Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 382.12,
          "end": 384.02,
          "en": "in the different parts of the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 384.02,
          "end": 386.19,
          "en": "we have to go back to store JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 386.19,
          "end": 390.97,
          "en": "and here we should import our favoritesReducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 390.97,
          "end": 394.92,
          "en": "which is that default export from this favorites file",
